			"Message": "refactor(Output): Apply semantic directory structure to build configuration and plugins\n\nComplete the reorganization of the Output element's build pipeline by migrating all source artifacts and ESBuild plugins into a nested, PascalCase directory hierarchy. This change applies the structural pattern established in the previous Source reorganization to the compiled `Configuration/` and `Source/` output trees.\n\nKey modifications:\n• **Directory Restructuring**: Flatten files like `BuiltIn.js`, `ChromiumIPC.js`, and `CopyNodeModules.js` into semantic paths (e.g., `ESBuild/Exclude/Built/In.js`, `Plugin/Transform/Replace/Electron/IPC/Service.js`).\n• **Import Path Updates**: Update all relative import paths in `Index.ts`, `Pipeline.ts`, and individual plugin modules to reflect the new deep nesting.\n• **Export Refactoring**: Rename default exports from verbose CamelCase (e.g., `BuiltIn_default`) to concise PascalCase (e.g., `In_default`) to match the new file names.\n• **Asset Path Alignment**: Correct CSS injection paths (e.g., `Editor/GPU/Layer.css`) to match the new asset directory structure.\n\nThis ensures the compiled configuration tree strictly adheres to the CodeEditorLand naming conventions, matching the modularity of the Source code and preventing path resolution errors in the Tauri/WKWebView environment.",
